    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0189" n="93" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg93"/>

                <head>No. 58.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Partridge.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-03-22"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 22,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch, No. 33, of the 22d of
                    January last, relating to the return of destitute citizens of the United States
                    in Brazil to this country has been received.</p>
                <p>As you were informed in my dispatch No. 16, there is no appropriation from which
                    a sum to defray the passage of these persons to the United States can properly
                    be drawn.</p>
                <p>A naval vessel is expected soon to return from Brazil, on which some of them can
                    embark, under orders heretofore issued.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
